crt-pi shader — original source and license
==========================================

Original shader: crt-pi.glsl from libretro/glsl-shaders
Repository: https://github.com/libretro/glsl-shaders
Path: crt/shaders/crt-pi.glsl
Author: Copyright (C) 2015-2016 davej
License: GNU General Public License v2 (or later) — see header in crt-pi.glsl

This repository ships assets/shaders/crt-pi.vert and
assets/shaders/crt-pi.frag, both derived from crt-pi.glsl and retained
under the original GPL-2.0+ license (see header in crt-pi.glsl).

Project note (play-crt):
  This repository keeps the original GPL-2.0+ header intact in
  assets/shaders/crt-pi.vert and assets/shaders/crt-pi.frag and lists
  the shader under GPL-2.0+ in README.md. Both shipped files are derived
  from the GPL-2.0+ original and retain license obligations. The Rust port
  in src/crt_pi.rs implements the same algorithm and is covered by the
  project's MIT license (algorithm itself is not copyrightable; the GLSL
  text remains GPL-2.0+).

  If you redistribute the .vert/.frag verbatim, you must comply with GPL-2.0+.
  If you only use the Rust port (CPU fallback), note that the glow path
  loads assets/shaders/crt-pi.vert and assets/shaders/crt-pi.frag at
  runtime and thus has a runtime dependency on the GPL-2.0+ shader text.

See also: https://github.com/libretro/glsl-shaders/blob/master/crt/shaders/crt-pi.glsl
